<Base title="Privacy" description="How the BORGAS website handles browsing and inquiry information."><section class="section"><div class="wrap reading"><p class="eyebrow">Website information</p><h1>Privacy.</h1><p>Updated September 16, 2026.</p><h2>Browsing this website</h2><p>BORGAS does not add analytics or advertising trackers to this website. Fonts and product images are served with the site.</p><p>The public website is hosted on GitHub Pages. Hosting and network providers may process technical request information, such as IP addresses, to deliver and protect the site. Their own privacy policies apply to their services.</p><h2>Product inquiries</h2><p>Where an email contact option is available, information you enter stays in the page until you choose to open an email draft. The site does not store the form contents or submit them to a server. Your email application and email provider handle the message when you send it.</p><p>BORGAS uses information you send to respond to your question and handle related support. Please include only the information needed for your request. An inquiry does not sign you up for marketing.</p><h2>Shopping and customer accounts</h2><p>Your cart is stored in your browser on this device. It contains product identifiers and quantities, and can be cleared by removing the products or clearing site data. If browser storage is blocked, the cart may not persist.</p><p>Supabase processes passwordless email sign-in and stores a session in your browser. Signing out removes that session. The BORGAS order service processes your account identifier, email address, delivery information, purchased items, totals, payment status and fulfillment status to handle orders and support.</p><p>Checkout is currently limited to a clearly labeled PayPal Sandbox test. Sandbox payments use test accounts and do not charge real money or create shipments. When real checkout opens, PayPal will process payment details; BORGAS will receive the payment and transaction status but will not collect your card number through this website.</p><p>Order information is retained as needed to handle purchases, support, refunds, disputes and required business records. Contact BORGAS about access or deletion requests; some records may need to be retained where required for payment, tax or legal purposes.</p><h2>External links</h2><p>Software release links open GitHub. External services have their own privacy practices. Review them before sharing information or downloading files.</p><h2>Questions</h2><p>Use the contact options shown on the <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a> for questions about your information.</p></div></section></Base>
